\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Illustration of the Generalized Pareto Distribution shape parameter $\xi $ and its interpretation. Left: $\xi <0$ (bounded tail, hard maximum on dependency distance, typical of tightly structured languages). Center: $\xi =0$ (exponential decay, no power-law behavior). Right: $\xi >0$ (unbounded power-law tail, possibility of very long dependencies, typical of flexible-order languages). The shape parameter directly captures tail heaviness independent of mean distance.}}{3}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:evt_illustration}{{1}{3}{Illustration of the Generalized Pareto Distribution shape parameter $\xi $ and its interpretation. Left: $\xi <0$ (bounded tail, hard maximum on dependency distance, typical of tightly structured languages). Center: $\xi =0$ (exponential decay, no power-law behavior). Right: $\xi >0$ (unbounded power-law tail, possibility of very long dependencies, typical of flexible-order languages). The shape parameter directly captures tail heaviness independent of mean distance}{figure.1}{}}
